PaperOrchestra Skills
Copyright 2026 the paper-orchestra-skills contributors

This repository is an independent, skill-native port of PaperOrchestra:
  PaperOrchestra: A Multi-Agent Framework for Automated AI Research Paper Writing
  Yiwen Song, Yale Song, Tomas Pfister, Jinsung Yoon
  Google Cloud AI Research
  https://github.com/google-research/paper-orchestra
  Copyright 2026 Google LLC
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The following material is adapted from that repository and remains under the
Apache License, Version 2.0:
  - the five-stage pipeline design and agent responsibilities;
  - outline, literature review, section writing, content refinement, and
    plotting prompt directives;
  - the citation verification policy, reviewer rubric, and evaluation concepts;
  - the CVPR 2025 and ICLR 2025 template bundles under
    skills/paper-template/assets/templates/.

The conference style files (*.sty, *.bst) are the official files distributed
with each venue's author kit and remain subject to their original terms. Their
copyright headers are preserved.

The scripts in this repository are a clean-room reimplementation using the
Python standard library unless a dependency is explicitly documented.

Third-party skills (MIT License)
--------------------------------
The following skills under skills/ are adapted from MIT-licensed projects. Each
SKILL.md ends with an Attribution section naming its source path and commit.
The full upstream license texts are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/.

  From Orchestra-Research/AI-Research-SKILLs
  (Copyright (c) 2025 Claude AI Research Skills Contributors):
    - skills/research-autoresearch
    - skills/research-brainstorming
    - skills/research-creative-thinking
    - skills/research-conference-talks
    - skills/research-systems-paper-writing

  From K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills (Copyright (c) 2025 K-Dense Inc.):
    - skills/research-experimental-design
    - skills/research-statistical-power

Changes: folders and `name` fields were prefixed with `research-`, long
descriptions were quoted for strict YAML parsers, and cross-references to skills
not present in this repository were retargeted. The systems-paper templates and
USENIX style files under skills/research-systems-paper-writing/templates/ keep
their original headers and terms. The research-experimental-design and
research-statistical-power scripts need numpy, pandas, scipy and statsmodels;
this is the only place the repository depends on third-party Python packages.
